# Depot NixOS Service Template

Rules for creating new NixOS services following the depot standard structure.

<rule>
name: nixos_service_template
description: Standards for creating new NixOS services
filters:
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "services/.*/machine/.*\\.nix$"
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "services/.*/machine/README\\.md$"
actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      Follow this standard structure for new NixOS services:

      1. Create these files under services/YOUR_SERVICE/machine/:
         - default.nix (main entry point)
         - vm.nix (VM/ISO configuration)
         - test.nix (test suite)
         - README.md (documentation)

      2. Use these file templates:

      default.nix:
      ```nix
      # Copyright (c) YEAR Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
      # SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary

      { depot, pkgs, ... }:

      with depot.nix.harmonia;

      let
        machine = import ./vm.nix { inherit depot pkgs; };

        # Extract just the hash part from the store path
        isoHash = builtins.substring 11 32 (toString machine.iso);
        isoName = builtins.baseNameOf (toString machine.iso);
      in
      {
        # Default package should be the VM
        default = machine.vm;

        # Individual components
        vm = machine.vm;
        iso = machine.iso;
        url = getIsoUrl machine.iso;

        tests = import ./test.nix { inherit depot pkgs; };

        meta.ci.targets = [
          "vm"
          "iso"
          "url"
        ];
      }
      ```

      vm.nix:
      ```nix
      # Copyright (c) YEAR Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
      # SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary

      { depot, pkgs, ... }:

      let
        nixosSystem = (import (pkgs.path + "/nixos/lib/eval-config.nix") {
          system = builtins.currentSystem;
          pkgs = pkgs;
          modules = [
            ({ modulesPath, pkgs, ... }: {
              imports = [
                (modulesPath + "/virtualisation/qemu-vm.nix")
                (modulesPath + "/installer/cd-dvd/iso-image.nix")
              ];

              system.stateVersion = "24.11";

              # Set empty root password for development
              users.users.root.initialPassword = "";

              virtualisation = {
                memorySize = 2048;
                cores = 2;
                graphics = false;
              };

              # Add your service configuration here
              services.YOUR_SERVICE = {
                enable = true;
                # Add service-specific configuration
              };

              # Configure networking if needed
              networking.firewall.allowedTCPPorts = [ ];

              isoImage.makeEfiBootable = true;
              isoImage.makeUsbBootable = true;
            })
          ];
        }).config;
      in
      {
        vm = nixosSystem.system.build.vm;
        iso = nixosSystem.system.build.isoImage;
      }
      ```

      test.nix:
      ```nix
      # Copyright (c) YEAR Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
      # SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary

      let
        nixpkgs = import <nixpkgs> {
          config = {
            allowUnfree = true;
          };
        };
      in
      import (nixpkgs.path + "/nixos/tests/make-test-python.nix") (
        { pkgs, ... }: {
          name = "YOUR_SERVICE";

          nodes.machine = { config, pkgs, ... }: {
            nixpkgs.config.allowUnfree = true;
            virtualisation.memorySize = 2048;
            virtualisation.cores = 2;

            # Add your service configuration here
            services.YOUR_SERVICE = {
              enable = true;
              # Add service-specific configuration
            };
          };

          testScript = ''
            start_all()

            # Wait for service to start
            machine.wait_for_unit("YOUR_SERVICE.service")

            # Add your test cases here
            machine.succeed("systemctl is-active YOUR_SERVICE.service")
          '';
        }
      )
      ```

      README.md:
      ```markdown
      <!--
       Copyright (c) YEAR Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
       SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary
      -->

      # YOUR_SERVICE Machine

      A NixOS VM configuration for running YOUR_SERVICE.

      ## Usage

      Build and run the VM:
      ```bash
      depot build //services/YOUR_PATH/machine
      depot run //services/YOUR_PATH/machine
      ```

      Build specific components:
      ```bash
      # Build the ISO
      depot build //services/YOUR_PATH/machine:iso

      # Run the tests
      depot test //services/YOUR_PATH/machine:tests
      ```

      ## Getting the ISO URL

      To get the URL where the ISO is stored:
      ```bash
      # This will output the URL where the ISO can be downloaded
      depot eval //services/YOUR_PATH/machine:url
      ```

      The URL is generated using Harmonia's storage system and can be used to download the ISO from any machine with appropriate access.
      ```

examples:
  - input: |
      services/myapp/machine/
      ├── default.nix
      ├── vm.nix
      ├── test.nix
      └── README.md
    output: "Correctly structured NixOS service"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>
```

This rule provides a template for creating new NixOS services with:

1. A consistent file structure
2. Standard boilerplate for VM/ISO creation
3. Basic test framework setup
4. Documentation template
5. Proper license headers
6. Integration with depot build system

The templates are generalized versions of the Vault service files, with placeholders like YOUR_SERVICE and YOUR_PATH that developers can replace with their specific service details.
